        "payload": {
          "description": "THE OPPORTUNITY\nCasechek is on a mission to innovate the implant supply chain and bring greater transparency to the cost of patient care. From procurement to payment, Casechek automates workflows for vendor-supported surgical procedures. Our emergent Bill Only solution provides a comprehensive system of record for hospitals and health systems to manage the complexity of surgical cases involving implantable medical devices, expose hidden expenses, and surface revenue opportunities.\nIn this role, you will design, build, and improve the technology that powers Casechek’s mobile and web products. As a Software Engineer, you will develop scalable cloud-based solutions, contribute to technical architecture and design decisions, and help translate product goals into reliable software. You will collaborate closely with Product, Engineering, and other internal teams to deliver solutions that meet customer and business needs. You will also help strengthen our development practices, code quality, testing standards, and overall technical capabilities.\nYour day-to-day interactions will require strategic thinking, strong communication skills, the ability to leverage data, and comfort managing complex initiatives. You should be adept at navigating new technologies and collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver exceptional service and support.\nCasechek is a highly collaborative environment, and our team is also self-motivated and works independently. We strongly believe that great ideas are not created in isolation. Our team interacts with our healthcare customers to understand their needs and ultimately deliver the best user experience possible.\nAbout Us\nCasechek is based out of Chicago’s Fulton Market, but we’re a hybrid, remote, and in-person team.\nWe are highly motivated and passionate about solving healthcare’s messiest problems with new technologies.\nWe value diversity, curiosity, and a passion for learning. The team has a lot of advanced degrees and even a few professional musicians.\nInnovating the implant supply chain is a marathon and not a sprint. We support each other in long-term growth and value developing transferable skills.\nResponsibilities\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, a related field, or equivalent professional experience required.\n5+ years of professional backend software development experience.\nStrong proficiency with TypeScript and Node.js.\nProfessional experience developing applications with NestJS.\nExperience designing, developing, and integrating REST APIs.\nExperience supporting and troubleshooting an AWS-hosted SaaS product.\nExperience building scalable, performant, and reliable software solutions.\nFamiliarity with relational database technologies, data modeling, and database design.\nExperience working in an Agile or Scrum software development environment.\nStrong problem-solving skills and the ability to address complex technical challenges creatively.\nSharp attention to detail and a commitment to writing clean, maintainable, and reliable code.\nExcellent English verbal and written communication skills.\nAbility to collaborate effectively across technical and nontechnical teams.\nAbility to manage multiple priorities and adapt to changing project requirements in a fast-paced environment.\nCommitment to continuous learning and staying current with modern technologies, frameworks, and development practices.\nRequirements\nRequirements\n5-8+ years of experience in B2B SaaS growth marketing, demand generation, or revenue marketing.\nDemonstrated track record of generating qualified pipeline and marketing-influenced revenue in support of an enterprise sales organization.\nStrong analytical and reporting skills, with comfort owning metrics such as qualified pipeline generated, opportunities created, conversion rates, campaign performance, and ROMI.\nHands-on expertise with CRM software and Marketing Automation (Salesforce and Pardot preferred), including lead management and attribution.\nAbility to operate strategically while remaining highly hands-on as an individual contributor.\nExperience in managing 1-3 direct reports is strongly preferred\nExperience in Healthcare strongly preferred: Healthcare Technology, Healthcare Supply Chain, Revenue Cycle, Medical Devices, or Hospital Operations.\nComfortable with MS Excel (analyzing spreadsheets and charts) as well as Microsoft PowerPoint.\nBachelor's degree in Marketing, Business Administration or relevant field. (MBA preferred).\nTech Stack\nNestJS\nAngular\nTypeScript\nNode.js\nPostgreSQL\nAWS\nAWS Lambda\n#Casechek\nBenefits\nWhy You'll Love Working Here\nCompetitive Salary and Annual Bonus\nThe salary range for this role is $100,000 to $125,000 , based on experience, skills, and location.\nOpportunity for Long-Term Incentives (LTI)\nBe part of our success with equity or long-term incentive plans that grow with the company.\n401(k) Match\nInvest in your future with our generous matching program to help you build long-term financial security.\nWork-from-Home Flexibility\nEnjoy the freedom to work where you are most productive with a supportive hybrid option in Chicago or a remote setup nationally.\nFlexible Time Off (Unlimited PTO)\nRecharge and focus on what matters most with unlimited paid time off tailored to your needs.\nParental Leave\nTake time to bond with and care for your growing family with fully paid parental leave options.\nComprehensive Medical and Dental Benefits\nPrioritize your health and well-being with premium plans for you and your family.\nBrand-New Pro-Level Laptop\nReceive top-tier tools and technology to set you up for success from day one.\nAnnual Education Budget\nExpand your skills and knowledge with dedicated funding for courses, certifications, and learning resources.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485031007": {
