        "fetched_at": "2026-11-06T23:16:19.566404+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nT-Rex Solutions, LLC is a proven mid-tier federal services provider established in 1999. We deliver data-centric mission services that help government customers secure, manage, and make effective use of information. Our teams design, integrate, secure, and deploy technology solutions supporting critical federal objectives. T-Rex provides services to numerous federal agencies and specializes in cloud and infrastructure services, cybersecurity, and big data engineering.\nWe believe strong customer outcomes begin with talented employees. T-Rex is committed to creating a collaborative culture that supports professional development and employee well-being. We are seeking a motivated early-career Web Developer to join our team supporting an Intelligence Community program in the Fort Meade, Maryland area.\nAbout The Role\nAs a fully cleared Web Developer, you will join a small, hardworking team building and supporting enterprise web-based services deployed in AWS. This entry-level opportunity is designed for someone who is ready to learn and grow as a software engineer. You will receive close mentorship, work on clearly scoped assignments, and develop sound engineering habits through documentation, collaboration, and code reviews.\nYou will contribute to the team’s development workflow while learning its codebase and deployment processes. No prior professional software engineering experience is required; relevant academic or personal projects can demonstrate your skills. Candidates presenting academic or personal projects must provide work samples.\nQualifications\nRequired qualifications include a bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related discipline from an accredited college or university. Four years of software engineering experience on projects using similar software processes may be substituted for the degree. No additional demonstrated experience is required.\nYou must hold an active, transferable U.S. government-issued TS/SCI clearance with Full Scope Polygraph (FSP). You must also meet DoD 8570.01 requirements with a minimum IAM Level I certification, such as CAP, GSLC, or Security+.\nApplicants should have professional, academic, or personal-project experience with one or more of the following: PHP, .NET/C#, Java, JavaScript, Python, HTML, CSS, or React. Comfort working in Linux environments is preferred, including familiarity with command-line basics, files, and permissions; candidates who are prepared to learn quickly are encouraged to apply.\nHelpful experience includes relational databases such as MariaDB, Microsoft SQL Server, MySQL, or Oracle; basic SQL; web or application servers such as Nginx, Apache, or Tomcat; and cloud concepts in AWS or Azure. Scripting with PowerShell or Python is also useful. We value clear written and verbal communication, teamwork, receptiveness to feedback, curiosity, and an interest in Agile practices.\nResponsibilities\nWith guidance from experienced teammates, you will implement well-defined features and bug fixes based on tickets and acceptance criteria. You will learn the team’s codebase, development practices, and deployment workflow while contributing to an enterprise web services platform.\nYou will also help maintain and troubleshoot web applications deployed in AWS by checking basic application health, reviewing logs, reproducing issues, and escalating problems when appropriate. You will communicate progress, ask thoughtful questions, follow documentation, participate in team activities, and apply feedback from code reviews to strengthen your engineering skills.\nBenefits\nT-Rex offers a diverse, collaborative workplace with opportunities for professional growth. Benefits include competitive compensation, performance bonuses, paid time off available upon joining (prorated based on start date), paid parental leave, and individual and family health, vision, and dental coverage. Employees may also access an annual training and professional development budget, tuition reimbursement, and a Transamerica 401(k) plan with company matching, fully vested after 60 days of employment.\nThe annual base salary range is $180,000–$230,000. This range is a general guideline; offers may reflect responsibilities, relevant experience, education, skills, internal equity, and market and business considerations.\nEqual Opportunity\nT-Rex Solutions is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, religion, color, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, parental status, national origin, age, disability, family medical history or genetic information, political affiliation, military service, or other non-merit-based factors.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487059085": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-06T23:16:19.566404+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Han IT Staffing is seeking a skilled Node.js Developer to build and support cloud-based applications for customer interactions. This role is suited to an engineer who enjoys developing secure serverless solutions and connecting contact center platforms with enterprise systems. You will contribute to intelligent interactive voice response (IVR) and self-service experiences using AWS technologies.\nAbout The Company\nHan IT Staffing connects organizations with technology professionals who help deliver business-critical solutions. For this opportunity, the developer will work on an AWS-based contact center platform, collaborating with technical teams and business stakeholders to create reliable, customer-focused digital experiences. The work supports the integration of contact center services with APIs, CRM platforms, and backend systems.\nAbout The Role\nAs a Node.js Developer, you will design, develop, test, deploy, and support serverless applications, with a primary focus on AWS Lambda. You will build and enhance workflows using Amazon Connect and Amazon Lex, and develop integrations that enable secure information exchange between contact center services and enterprise applications. You will take part in the software development lifecycle, from technical design and implementation through testing, deployment, troubleshooting, and documentation. Success in this role requires practical Node.js and AWS experience, sound engineering judgment, and the ability to work collaboratively across teams.\nQualifications\nA bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related discipline is preferred; equivalent professional experience may also be considered. Candidates should have at least three years of Node.js development experience and at least two years of hands-on AWS development experience. Demonstrated experience developing and deploying AWS Lambda functions is required. Experience with Amazon Connect and/or Amazon Lex is important for building contact center workflows.\nYou should have strong knowledge of RESTful APIs, JSON, and microservices architecture, along with experience integrating applications with databases, CRM systems, and third-party services. Familiarity with AWS services such as API Gateway, DynamoDB, S3, CloudWatch, IAM, SNS, SQS, and EventBridge is valuable. Experience with Git, GitHub, and CI/CD pipelines is expected. You should also bring strong debugging and performance optimization skills, an understanding of cloud security principles, and the ability to communicate technical information clearly.\nResponsibilities\nDesign, develop, maintain, and improve Node.js applications running on AWS Lambda. Build and enhance IVR and self-service workflows with Amazon Connect and Amazon Lex. Create integrations between contact center platforms and enterprise applications, databases, CRM systems, and third-party APIs. Develop reusable Lambda services for authentication, routing, customer identification, case management, and self-service transactions.\nBuild RESTful APIs and event-driven solutions using appropriate AWS services. Apply secure coding practices, including authentication, authorization, encryption, and data protection controls. Contribute to CI/CD pipelines and deployment automation using GitHub and AWS DevOps services. Write and maintain automated unit, integration, and regression tests. Investigate production issues and improve application performance, scalability, and reliability. Collaborate with architects, contact center engineers, QA teams, and business stakeholders, and maintain technical documentation, deployment procedures, and operational runbooks.\nBenefits\nThis opportunity offers the chance to work with modern AWS serverless technologies and contribute to customer-facing contact center solutions. You will collaborate with cross-functional teams, develop expertise in cloud integrations, and support applications used for intelligent self-service experiences. Compensation, benefits, work arrangements, and other employment details can be discussed during the hiring process.\nEqual Opportunity\nHan IT Staffing is committed to fair and inclusive hiring. Qualified candidates will be considered without discrimination on the basis of legally protected characteristics. We value diverse perspectives and encourage applicants whose experience and skills align with the role to apply.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488038613": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-06T23:16:19.566404+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Careers\nEngineering\nLahore, Pakistan (Hybrid)\nFull-time\n3+ years\nResponsibilities\nDevelop native C++ and C# Windows desktop applications\nImplement driver communication via IOCTL and shared memory\nBuild system services and monitoring utilities\nOwn the user experience of hardware control interfaces\nSkills\nC++\nC#\nWin32\nWPF\nCOM\nPreferred Skills\nWinUI\nETW\nCredential Providers\nofficial@haemantech.com",
